title: Romans 2:1-11 – The Inescapable Judgment
description: Romans 2:1-11: the inexcusable judge, the treasury of wrath, judgment by deeds, and no respect of persons.

output: lessons/romans/romans-2.html

# Converted from romans-2-romasn2-1.html, section for section. Quoted words are corrected to the KJV.

=== Romans 2:1-11
--- Romans 2:1-11: The Inescapable Judgment [title]
overline: Week 3
heading: ROMANS 2:1-11
sub: The Inescapable Judgment

--- 1. The Inexcusable Judge
kicker: Romans 2:1-4
refs: Romans 2:1-4
callout-honest: Paul is shifting his **diatribe** (a logical argument to persuade) from the Reprobate (Rom 1) to the person who would judge them, using the hypothetical **Interlocutor** (“O man”).
panel: The Condemnation of the Judge | “Therefore thou art **inexcusable**, O man, whosoever thou art that judgest”.
panel: You Condemn Yourself | “for wherein thou judgest another, **thou condemnest thyself**”.
panel: The Judge Commits the Same Sins | “for thou that judgest **doest the same things**”.

--- The Inexcusable Judge (continued)
kicker: Romans 2:1-4
panel: The Concept of Wrath for Sin | Paul used the **extreme case of Reprobates** to establish the concept of wrath for sin. Recognizing the wrath of God against the reprobates means **we who do any of the same are just as guilty**.
panel: All are Accountable | Paul established that even **heathens know enough about God to be held accountable**.
panel: God is Just | “But we are sure that the **judgment of God is according to truth** against them which commit such things”.

--- 2. The Treasury of Wrath
kicker: Romans 2:5-6
refs: Romans 2:5-6
lead: Paul is introducing a concept of judgment similar to **accounting or bookkeeping**. The sinner who persists in sin is actively building a record with God, not escaping.
panel: You Cannot Escape | “If you think you aren’t subject to the same wrath as the worst reprobate, you are wrong. **None shall escape the judgment of God**”.
panel: The Sinner Builds an Account | The sinner “builds up an account with God”.
panel: Storing Up Wrath | “Thou... **treasurest up unto thyself wrath** against the day of wrath and revelation of the righteous judgment of God”.
panel: The Final Standard | God will judge all men: “**Who will render to every man according to his deeds**”.

--- 3. Judgment by Deeds and Recompense
kicker: Romans 2:6-9
refs: Romans 2:6-9
lead: Just as the Reprobate receives the appropriate recompense for their error, so too does every man.
table: CONDUCT (The Deeds) | RECOMPENSE (The Judgment)
tr: **Patient Continuance in Well Doing** (Seeking for glory and honour and immortality) | **Eternal Life**
tr: **Contentious**, and do not **obey the truth**, but obey **unrighteousness** | **Indignation and Wrath**, **Tribulation and Anguish**

--- 4. No Respect of Persons
kicker: Romans 2:9-11
refs: Romans 2:9-11
lead: Paul introduces another key theme of the Epistle to the Romans: **Jews and Gentiles are all treated the same by God**.
panel: Wrath or Peace for All | Wrath or peace is given “to the **Jew first, and also to the Gentile** (Greek)”.
panel: The Final Rule | “For there is **no respect of persons with God**”.
